lilles","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lilles/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T10:04:37Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T10:04:37Z","body":"As @Loirooriol points out, this is not just limited to `<length>` values.\n\nAssume `--number` is a registered custom property with the `<number>` syntax:\n\n```css\np {\n  --number: calc(10 + 2 * sign(1em - 20px));\n  font-size: calc(var(--number) * 2px);\n}\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/2939410532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/2963465791","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9517#issuecomment-2963465791","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9517","id":2963465791,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM6wouY_","user":{"login":"css-meeting-bot","id":27466577,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDY2NTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27466577?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/css-meeting-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T16:27:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T16:27:16Z","body":"The CSS Working Group just discussed `[css-properties-values-api-1] Figure out what to do with font-relative lengths`.\n\n<details><summary>The full IRC log of that discussion</summary>\n&lt;JoshT> TabAtkins: the deal here is that if you have registered custom properties. we resolve unit math.<br>\n&lt;JoshT> ... if you have an em, this now depends on the font-size property<br>\n&lt;JoshT> ... I have proposal to add constaints to length type custom properties<br>\n&lt;fantasai> what constraints?<br>\n&lt;JoshT> ... not yet complete. number typed ones could also get this from algebra<br>\n&lt;JoshT> ... this doesn't require any resolutions<br>\n&lt;JoshT> ... I need to a: extend this to apply to all typed custom properties<br>\n&lt;JoshT> ... b: reqrite to use the new dependency mapping property that is in all the new CSS specs<br>\n&lt;JoshT> ... will just be a mechanical transform, but I think there's a solution. just need to take care of it now<br>\n&lt;JoshT> fantasai: I don't understand why it was brought up to the WG<br>\n&lt;fantasai> s/WG/WG if not going to even explain what we're doing/<br>\n&lt;JoshT> TabAtkins: was brought up by oriall. I'm just acknowledging that it is being worked on<br>\n&lt;TabAtkins> s/oriall/oriol/<br>\n&lt;oriol> I didn't remember adding this to agenda, happy to wait for Tab's edits<br>\n&lt;fantasai> ok, that was a really long way to say \"let's take this off the agenda until futher work\"<br>\n&lt;JoshT> astearns: so we'll take it off the agenda and keep the issue open. will bring it back when Tab has done some work<br>\n</details>\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/2963465791/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]